Generic single-database configuration.
## Database setup

The app uses SQLite locally (a file called `workflow_runner.db`, created automatically) and PostgreSQL for a hosted demo.

Build or update your database after cloning, and again after pulling changes that add migrations:

```
alembic upgrade head
```

To start from scratch locally, delete `workflow_runner.db` and run the command again.

After changing a model, create a new migration, check the generated file in `migrations/versions/`, then apply it:

```
alembic revision --autogenerate -m "describe the change"
alembic upgrade head
```

Set `DATABASE_URL` to point at another database. See `.env.example` for the variables.

### Troubleshooting

If importing SQLAlchemy fails on Windows with "An Application Control policy has blocked this file", delete the compiled files inside your virtual environment and try again:

```
Get-ChildItem .venv\Lib\site-packages\sqlalchemy -Recurse -Filter *.pyd | Remove-Item
```

## API

See `docs/api-examples.md` for the endpoints with example requests and responses.